<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wafd Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–1952</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wafd was an Egyptian nationalist party that grew out of the delegation (wafd) led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saad-zaghloul">Saad Zaghloul</a> in 1918 to demand independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. The most popular party of the monarchy, it won most free elections between 1924 and 1950 and negotiated the Anglo-Egyptian Treaty of 1936. It was dissolved after the 1952 revolution and revived in 1978 as the New Wafd.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wafd-party.jpg" alt="Wafd Party" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wafd Party (Life time: 1919-1952) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wafd_Party_logo.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
